   "confidence": "low",
   "notes": "Joshua Taylor Building, 59 Sidney St (Units A-C). Three fronts under one roof: south unit (ex-Monsoon in photos, OSM POI now Pizza Pilgrims) with large dark-framed plate-glass shopfront and pale upper floors; Superdrug middle unit in red brick with stone dressings, brick pilaster strips and round-arched second-floor windows over a white shopfront with dark fascia; north corner unit (David Clulow) white-painted brick with moulded architraves, cornice hoods on the first-floor windows and arched shopfront glazing under a green fascia. Single wall material can't express the three finishes; red brick chosen as dominant. Window counts per unit estimated from oblique views."
